  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">She Leads EA 21-25: Advancing GYW rights to meaningful participation and engagement in regional decision making spaces.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While African WROs do  recognize the specific oppressions that the girl-child faces, the voices of GYW have hardly been integrated in a meaningful manner in the women&#x2019;s rights movement, nor adequately represented in the regional decision making spaces. This is partly because WROs assume that they represent all female interests, and also the fact that most GYW lack the capacity to access relevant platforms. This is a reflection of the effects of negative cultural norms, lack of resources, and inadequate strategies to meaningfully engage them.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="22">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Horn of Africa Youth Network</narrative>
  </participating-org>
